      "details": "After key publication and successful metadata close, records probe-intent, awaits probe.run, and records probe-completed only after currentness and confirmed close. Catch returns ok:false; close retains cleanup debt. No qualified rejection is fabricated."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Outer probe cancellation is a distinct original30s signal and includes startup.",
      "source": "OpenCodeV2ModelProbe.ts",
      "blob": "195dabe664b14a2fe5c231e137690db6126c0e05",
      "lines": [
        63,
        64,
        341,
        350
      ],
      "details": "Ordinary credential profile uses modelProbeTimeoutMs30000 from original credentials fixture line426. run sets deadline and combined signal before start(combined). activeSignal makes later currentness false on cancellation."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The outer signal reaches already admitted native HTTP only through injected fetch; pending custody uses its own original signal.",
      "source": "OpenCodeV2ModelProbe.ts",
      "lines": [
        151,
        179,
        285,
        309
      ],
      "details": "beforeRequest reserves an owned lease before native custody await and releases it on failure. assertCurrent checks activeSignal and deadline. fetchImpl combines the start signal, Host abort and the provider request signal only at actual fetch. The source comment explicitly preserves original custody drain."
    },
    {
      "finding": "No existing typed driver signal/deadline input can be wired from the app.",
      "source": "archived v2-driver-config.d.ts / driver-session.js / v2-driver-native.js",
      "lines": {
        "config": [
          6,
          24
        ],
        "driver": [
          14,
          35
        ],
        "native": [
          18,
          19,
          48
        ]
      },
      "details": "Driver config explicitly Omit<TransportConfig,deadline|signal>; Session creates its own controller and passes that to its protocol. Native wireConfig explicitly overrides signal and deadline from its own scope. Merely adding unknown fields to the app object is not an existing public contract and would not replace these native values."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The recorded read flags cannot exclude outer probe expiry.",
      "source": "archived v2-native-cut.js",
      "lines": [
        146,
        158,
        170,
        196
      ],
      "details": "Diagnostic deadlineExpired/aborted are recorded against native cut/request signals before local self-abort. They do not observe the combined signal inside the Host fetch wrapper. Exact original after-log transport_failure has those inner flags false."
    },
    {
      "finding": "A failure of one final observation may leave the sibling with independently uncertain cleanup.",
      "source": "archived v2-native-cut.js / v2-execution-transport.js",
      "lines": {
        "cut": [
          254,
          274,
          311,
          348
        ],
        "transport": [
          300,
          363
        ]
      },
      "details": "Both final independent reads are joined with Promise.allSettled. First failure aborts the cut; any sibling cleanup-unknown takes precedence in the returned exception while diagnostics retain the first failing fact. Transport disposal separately joins tracked HTTP/stream work. The retained first-event record does not reveal the final thrown branch."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Required unknown is sticky across physical stop; close has several closed failure branches.",
      "source": "archived v2-driver-native.js / driver-session.js",
      "lines": {
        "native": [
          32,
          46,
          62,
          78,
          202,
          211
        ],
        "driver": [
          161,
          183
        ]
      },
      "details": "A read cleanup-unknown or wire.dispose rejection latches cleanupUnknown. Driver.close waits loop/control/replies, protocol.dispose and confirmStopped under original bounds; it returns unknown for any caught branch or false stop result. Host subsequently attempts server.stopOwned independently; that cannot erase a prior unconfirmed driver close."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Interrupt is an existing native control action, not a missing signal parameter.",
      "source": "OpenCodeV2ModelProbe.ts / archived driver-session.js / v2-driver-backend.js",
      "lines": {
        "probe": [
          281,
          308,
          365,
          380
        ],
        "driver": [
          119,
          152
        ],
        "backend": [
          7,
          24
        ]
      },
      "details": "The ordinary probe selects text-only capabilities and never requests interrupt. Session.interrupt reconciles the original native read, then may cancel inbox or invoke native interrupt; it needs fresh currentness/credentials. After the original probe deadline, Host admissions/readPassword reject. Adding early interrupt changes original native actions and timing; doing it after deadline requires authority that current contract does not grant."
    }
